{
  "case_id": "2006-06-278",
  "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "KENNETH W. STARR, ESQ., Los Angeles, Cal.; on behalf of Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule the Court -- that it articulated in Tinker. The rule of the Court as"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Disruptive of what? Disruptive of the classroom order? There was no classroom here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be disorderly? I don't understand this disorder. If somebody holds up a sign and says change the marijuana laws, why is it disruptive of anything, simply because the school quite naturally has said we support the enforcement of the law, and the law right now does forbid the use of marijuana."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The First Amendment does not require public school officials to stand aside and permit students who are entrusted to their supervision and care to promote or encourage the use of illegal drugs. As this Court observed in Earls, the nationwide drug - drug epidemic makes the war against drugs a pressing concern in every school."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And is that the rationale\non which you wish us to decide this case, nothing more\nbroad?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But that's a\nviewpoint-neutral regulation. This isn't, the principal\ndidn't say this was a viewpoint-neutral regulation, did\nshe?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Mertz",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MERTZ: I think it was clearly\nestablished at the time, Your Honor, that a principal\ncould not engage in viewpoint censorship of a\nnondisruptive expression, under both Ninth Circuit law\nand this Court's law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mertz",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe the answer is that the Tinker case as we understand it struck a very wise compromise between allowing school officials to have complete discretion to suppress student speech in order to maintain what they conceive of as their individual mission and the student's right to speak in a nondisruptive manner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think we're using disruption in two different senses here and we should probably separate the two. One sense is disrupting the class so that whatever is being taught can't be taught. But you're also using it in the sense of undermining a general message that the school is trying to get across: Obey the law, don't use drugs, whatever. Maybe we should have a different word for -- the first is disruption. Disruption is a, is a funny word for the second. Let's called it undermining instead."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mertz",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "motions for summary judgment in the district court, and there were no findings, actually no factual findings at all, and certainly nothing on that particular point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Superintendent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the rest of his behavior warranted the suspension."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Should the teacher have known, even in the, in the calm deliberative atmosphere of the school later, what the correct answer is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I ask to you clarify one thing. I initiated this line of questioning when I said I was surprised that your brief made such a big deal that he was late to school. You would still be making the argument about the free speech right if he had diligently showed up for his math class first period in the morning, gone out with the others, and had his banner to unfurl when the torch came by?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Even if the principal couldn't tell him to take down the manner even if she thought he was part of the school group reasonably, if he really wasn't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Mertz",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "pure free speech in a public place argument. That's the one that hinges on the fact that he was not among the released students. The other argument, which we believe in equally, is that even if it were a on-campus or on an extension of campus like a field trip, then under Tinker because it was not disruptive they cannot punish it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Starr",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For the reasons that have been discussed, under no circumstances should Deborah Morse, a conscientious principal, be subjected to the possibility of punitive damages or compensatory damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-278",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c06b7fcf940fa58ea3a9fa4f5703ba24f41fb0695b039015ebc57dffaa3e4725",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c06b7fcf940f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you counsel, the case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:04 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
